cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or these records, please cite the accompanying
  paper, "Amount, mechanism, and decision threshold in minority oversampling:
  a controlled evaluation of class-size-normalized local support" (submitted
  to Machine Learning). Until it is published, please cite this repository.
title: "N-LDF: amount, mechanism and decision threshold in minority oversampling"
abstract: >-
  Implementation, experiment records and analysis code for a controlled
  evaluation of minority oversampling. N-LDF is an oversampler built on a
  bounded, class-size-normalized local-support statistic; the paper uses it
  as a case for separating the effect of the oversampling mechanism from the
  effect of the amount of synthetic data and of the decision threshold.
  The repository holds the complete fold-level records of the benchmark
  (41 KEEL tasks, six strategies, four classifiers, 21,911 fits), of the
  controlled experiments on the same partitions (matched amounts,
  threshold-tuned and class-weighted baselines, further oversamplers,
  ablations and parameter sensitivity), of a held-out evaluation on 13 tasks
  from 10 further sources under a protocol hashed before the run, and of a
  re-run that reproduces the archived benchmark; one command regenerates
  every table and figure of the paper from these records.
type: software
